From 64260af84e8bcaddb6c67f2e6570a2573a4bea45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:53:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 101/105] vfio: nvtrace - per-BAR trapping and a binary trace
 of device accesses

New vfio-pci properties (on the vfio-pci base type, so vfio-user-pci has
them too):
  x-trap-bars=MASK   BARs that are never mmapped, so every guest access
                     traps to QEMU (default 0x1 with x-nvtrace, else 0)
  x-nvtrace=on       trace the device
  x-nvtrace-file=F   trace file (.zst/.lz4/.gz pipe through the compressor);
                     default $NVTRACE_MMIO
  x-nvtrace-irq=on   route MSI/MSI-X/INTx and ioeventfds through QEMU so
                     every interrupt and BAR write is seen (default on)
  x-nvtrace-gsp=on   NVIDIA FSP/GSP capture (default on, 10de display class)

Records: BAR accesses (direct, config mirror quirk, window quirk, ioeventfd,
emulated MSI-X table/PBA, expansion ROM), config space accesses, BAR
(re)programming, interrupts, MSI/MSI-X vector setup, resets and FLR, and
for NVIDIA GPUs the FSP EMEM packets, the GSP boot structures (FMC boot
params, WPR meta, libos args, GSP_ARGUMENTS_CACHED, queue page table, GSP
log buffers) and every GSP command/status queue RPC.
